# Trivy has its own ignore mechanism, separate from pnpm audit's
# `pnpm-workspace.yaml` -> `auditConfig.ignoreGhsas`. Kept consistent with
# that file's reasoning.
#
# 2026-07-26: re-investigated every entry that used to live here
# (CVE-2026-59892/propagator-jaeger, CVE-2026-59869/js-yaml v4,
# GHSA-f88m-g3jw-g9cj/sharp, GHSA-r28c-9q8g-f849/postcss) — all 4 had real
# fixes available (version bumps, not silent overrides; see
# pnpm-workspace.yaml for what changed and how each was verified) and are
# no longer accepted findings. Only one remains, now narrowly scoped rather
# than a blanket accept:
#
# CVE-2026-14257 (GHSA-mh99-v99m-4gvg): brace-expansion DoS via unbounded
# expansion length (fix >=5.0.8). Fixed for every consumer except one edge:
# minimatch@3.1.5 (pulled in by @eslint/config-array, @eslint/eslintrc, and
# @lhci/cli's chrome-launcher>rimraf>glob chain) hard-requires
# brace-expansion's old v1.x default-export-as-function shape — forcing v5
# there broke `pnpm lint` outright (confirmed live:
# `TypeError: expand is not a function`), and no v1.x release fixes this
# CVE (checked the full version list upstream). Dev-only lint/CI tooling,
# never reachable at runtime. Mirrors pnpm-workspace.yaml's scoped
# `minimatch@3.1.5>brace-expansion` override.
CVE-2026-14257
